  "node_source_commit": "3fe65982fd40462b4053d8e6757de3ec552e36be",
  "node_sources": [
    "x/shared/types/canonical.go:60-70 (typed scalar encoders Uint32BE/Uint64BE/BoolByte/EnumBE)",
    "x/shared/types/canonical.go:80-95 (CanonicalFrameBytes, the shared H_FIELDS_V1 framing primitive)",
    "x/shared/types/canonical.go:136-145 (CanonicalHashBytes: SHA256 over domain-prefixed frame)",
    "x/hub/types/testdata/hub_domains_v1.json:5-6 (frozen preimage layout and per-type field encoding, §1.2)",
    "x/hub/types/testdata/hub_domains_v1.json:7 (KNOWN ENCODING DRIFT for operator addresses)",
    "x/hub/types/hub_domains_fixture_test.go:101-106,128-131 (nested frame carries no domain prefix)"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "preimage = u64_be(len(domain)) || domain || for each field u64_be(len(field)) || field; digest = SHA-256(preimage).",
    "Field encoding: string = strict UTF-8 bytes; bytes = raw; hash = raw 32 bytes; uint32/uint64 = 4/8-byte big endian; bool = 0x00/0x01; enum = uint32 big endian; frame = nested field frame with no domain prefix.",
    "The CORTEX_HFIELDS_* domains are synthetic primitive-coverage domains. They are not contract domains and nothing signs them.",
    "The node_parity vectors are copied verbatim from x/hub/types/testdata/hub_domains_v1.json at the commit above. Their domains are Hub staking domains that Cortex never signs; they are present only so the framing primitive is proven byte-for-byte against the frozen contract. Do not reuse them as Cortex signing domains.",
    "No vector encodes an operator address or any Cortex message field vector. This package exposes no address field constructor because it is the framing primitive and carries no Bech32 decoder: callers resolve the address codec bytes themselves (internal/nodewire/address.go CanonicalOperatorAddressBytes) and pass them as hfields.Bytes. Concrete Cortex message field vectors live with the package that owns their field order - internal/nodewire/testdata/task_domains_v1.json and result_receipt_v1.json."
  ],
